REVIEW CRITERIA:
The Planning Commission’s role in adoption of the Urban Renewal Plan and Project is to review and
provide a recommendation to the Governing Body as to whether or not to approve per Wyo. Stat. § 15-
9-108. The specific review criteria is listed in Wyo. Stat. § 15-9-110 and is summarized in the attached
Hynds and Hole Urban Renewal Plan and Project document.

CONCLUSION:

Staff concludes that this Urban Renewal Plan and Project meets the applicable review criteria which is
outlined in the attached Urban Renewal Plan and Project document.

STAFF RECOMMENDATION:

Staff recommends the Planning Commission recommend approval of the Hynds and the Hole Urban
Renewal Plan and Project, noting the request meets the review criteria of Wyo. Stat. § 15-9-110.

URBAN RENEWAL AUTHORITY RECOMMENDATION:

The Urban Renewal Authority recommend approval of the Hynds and the Hole Urban Renewal Plan
and Project as presented by staff, subject to modifying the plan and project document to
remove references to condemnation, noting the Plan and Project conforms with Wyo. Stat. §
15-9-110, and authorized submission to the Planning Commission for review and recommendation
to the Governing Body.

